---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Update &amp; rollback — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Update &amp; rollback</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Update, rollback, refresh, and runtime releases. An update activates only
      a revision merged on the sum origin default branch, resolved to an
      immutable SHA.
    </p>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Update and roll back</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>./bin/sumctl update check          <span class="c"># fetch origin, resolve the merged revision, report default/active/compatibility</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl update apply          <span class="c"># stage the release, validate coexistence, switch .local/current, fast-forward a clean clone</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl update status</div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl update rollback       <span class="c"># reselect the recorded previous approved runtime; records, questions, reports, worktrees stay</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl update recover --generation GENERATION</div>
      </div>
      <p>Only the user authorizes update or rollback. An interrupted activation requires its exact journal generation. No core, agent or service is restarted, and dirty or diverged work stays intact. Normal Open/init/status never migrate schema-one state.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Refresh running sessions</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>./bin/sumctl refresh request               <span class="c"># coordinator contract plus every non-archived task</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl refresh status                <span class="c"># confirmed / submitted-unconfirmed / pending-busy / pending-unreachable / unreachable / capability-deferred</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl refresh adopt --coordinator rN</div>
      </div>
      <p>Refresh persists a sealed next revision before one eligible HC send. Qualified Codex uses Tab: idle has <code>if:idle</code>, observed Done sends without <code>if</code> or <code>force</code>, and a raced busy turn queues it for the next turn. This is not an atomic Done guard. Only a matching adoption receipt confirms application.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sec">
      <h2>Runtime releases</h2>
      <div class="codeblock">
        <div>./bin/sumctl release stage            <span class="c"># builds .local/releases/&lt;sha&gt; for HEAD; nothing is activated</span></div>
        <div>./bin/sumctl release list</div>
      </div>
      <p>A release holds the committed Sum tree, native helper, exact published HC 0.1.14, matched manual/template and checksummed manifest. Rollback checks actual target binary capabilities. Existing-installation cutover refuses without enforceable legacy writer/sender exclusion that current legacy APIs cannot prove; an old schema-one runtime cannot reactivate an inactive archive. No production migration is claimed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
